  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 119a645d648fe4a4c86c14f18251ec06, type: 3}
  m_Name: l1_marlo_first
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  presentation: 0
  lines:
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: Easy there, little one! You are a long way from any reef I know. I am Marlo.
      I have watched over these waters since before your grandparents hatched.
  - speaker: You
    portrait: {fileID: -4255054504167156931, guid: 24d008a2918cc544f87755498eae8b2b, type: 3}
    text: The storm took me. I do not know how to get home.
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: 'A storm-lost tang. It happens more than you would think. But there is
      a way: the Lantern Road.'
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: Long ago, the sea king lit a chain of ruins from this reef down to the
      deepest trench. Bring three Ancient Pearls to a ruin, and it wakes.
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: At the end of the road, in the Deep, sleeps the Golden Clam. Its light
      shines on every lost fish's home. Reach it, and you will see yours.
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: But you are small, and this sea is not kind to small fish. Eat what is
      smaller than you, grow strong, and stay away from the big ones.
  - speaker: Marlo
    portrait: {fileID: 5496424915399974395, guid: 07b2589218cdd3147bc544ac1e97088a, type: 3}
    text: Oh, and a bottle washed up beside the old wreck on the seabed. Bottles
      always carry stories. Go and have a look.
  choices: []
  flagToSetWhenFinished: metMentor
  abilityWhenFinished: 0
  journalTitle: 
